<%# The "Change animation" CTA on a card's left panel.

    Two card types have an animation to change and they are not the same
    animation: a Range card's is the reaction CHARACTER on this panel, an NPS
    card's is the liquid CONTAINER on the answer side. The control is the same
    control either way — one button, on the panel where every other "change
    this card's asset" CTA already lives, so a creator learns one place —
    so it is one partial rather than two near-identical buttons.

    Locals:
      action — the animation-picker method to open (`open` for a Range card's
               character sets, `openShapes` for an NPS card's containers)
%>
<button type="button" class="add-animation-fab"
        data-action="click->animation-picker#<%= action %>"
        title="<%= t("editor.change_animation_title", default: "Change this card's animation") %>">
  <span class="add-animation-fab-icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="3"></rect>
      <path d="M10 9l5 3-5 3z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></path>
    </svg>
  </span>
  <span><%= t("editor.change_animation", default: "Change animation") %></span>
</button>
